            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0371" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting Chairman of the American Delegation (Gibson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-01T18:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Your 293, July 1, 5 p.m. The point you have raised seems to be one of detail
                    suitable for adjustment in Geneva. It would not <pb facs="0372" n="252"
                        xml:id="pg252"/> seem necessary to modify your draft speech or re-calculate
                    the quantitative chart, unless you should perceive positive advantages in so
                    doing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
